THEOREM 1 — forward invariance of S° = (1/3, 2/3) under a hard Cantor
gate, for ARBITRARY disturbance amplitude.
Claim: h(t) = 1/2 + (h₀-1/2)e^{-αt} exactly, independent of δ.
============================================================================================
  4704 configurations tested (n=1..8, α∈{0.2,0.8,2}, A up to 1000, 7 waveforms, 7 h₀)
  trajectories that ever left S      : 0
  max gate value ever seen inside S  : 0.000e+00
  max |h(t) − linear solution|       : 2.776e-14   (RK4 truncation only)
  min R_safe over all configurations : 1.000000
  ⇒ Theorem 1 holds numerically: the disturbance amplitude is IRRELEVANT
    once the state is inside S°. Robustness there is an identity, not a finding.

