============================================================================================
  α = 0.2 :  f(1/3⁺) = +α/6 = +0.033333 ,  f(2/3⁻) = −α/6 = -0.033333
  α = 0.5 :  f(1/3⁺) = +α/6 = +0.083333 ,  f(2/3⁻) = −α/6 = -0.083333
  α = 0.8 :  f(1/3⁺) = +α/6 = +0.133333 ,  f(2/3⁻) = −α/6 = -0.133333
  α = 1.2 :  f(1/3⁺) = +α/6 = +0.200000 ,  f(2/3⁻) = −α/6 = -0.200000
  α = 2.0 :  f(1/3⁺) = +α/6 = +0.333333 ,  f(2/3⁻) = −α/6 = -0.333333

  gate ON the boundary points (closed-interval convention): g(1/3) = 1 , g(2/3) = 1
  gate just INSIDE: g(1/3+1e-12) = 0 , g(2/3-1e-12) = 0
  ⇒ the CLOSED set S is not invariant at the two endpoint states themselves;
    the OPEN set S° is. This distinction is why Theorem 1 is stated on S°.

