THEOREM 2 — robust invariance for a GENERAL gate:  B·g(∂S) < α/6 .
Tested on the smooth Cantor gate, where g(∂S) > 0 by construction.
============================================================================================
  configurations where Theorem 2 GUARANTEES invariance : 31
    of these, how many actually escaped S              : 0  (must be 0)
  configurations where the guarantee FAILS             : 97
    of these, how many actually escaped S              : 65  (67.0%)
  ⇒ the condition is SUFFICIENT, not necessary: many configurations that
    violate it still stay inside, because escape also requires crossing a
    leaky boundary layer of width ≈ ln(6A/α − 1)/β before the disturbance
    reverses sign.

